Roger starts with 14 books. The librarian takes 2 of them, so Roger has 14 - 2 = 12 books.  He can fit 3 books on a shelf. To find out how many shelves he needs, we need to divide the number of books by the number of books per shelf: 12 / 3 = 4.  Therefore, he needs 4 shelves.

\boxed{4}

